-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Louisiana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Louisiana</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Louisiana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Louisiana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights sale</li><li>Turn the Louisiana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Louisiana House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Louisiana statutes set the basic rules between landlords and tenants, including deposits, notices and what happens when a rental is sold.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Residential deposit must be returned within one month after the lease terminates; any retained portion requires an itemized statement within one month (or within 15 days after that month) after tenancy ends. (La. R.S. 9:3251(A); <a href='https://legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=107468' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Landlord may retain amounts reasonably necessary to remedy tenant default or unreasonable wear; tenant must furnish a forwarding address. (La. R.S. 9:3251(A); <a href='https://legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=107468' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>On transfer of the lessor&#x27;s interest, the deposit passes to the successor, who becomes responsible for its return. (La. R.S. 9:3251(B); <a href='https://legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=107468' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Month-to-month lease termination notice: ten calendar days before the end of the month; leases measured by periods longer than a month: 30 days. (La. C.C. Art. 2728; <a href='https://www.legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=109792' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Louisiana?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Louisiana houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/louisiana-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Louisiana Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/louisiana-eviction-notice/'>Louisiana 