tion:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Louisiana Eviction Notice Rules: Notice Types, Days and Selling the House</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Louisiana</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Louisiana Eviction Notice Rules: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Louisiana Eviction Notice Rules sale</li><li>Turn the Louisiana Eviction Notice Rules offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Louisiana House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Louisiana law requires a landlord to give a specific written notice before filing an eviction, and the number of days depends on the reason.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>For nonpayment, expiration or any other termination of the lease, lessor must deliver written notice to vacate allowing not less than five days from delivery. (La. C.C.P. Art. 4701; <a href='https://legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=112073' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>If the lease has no definite term, the notice required for its termination counts as the notice to vacate; for a definite term, notice to vacate may be given not more than 30 days before term expires. (La. C.C.P. Art. 4701; <a href='https://legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=112073' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Lessee may waive the notice to vacate by written waiver in the lease; lessor may then immediately file eviction proceedings. (La. C.C.P. Art. 4701; <a href='https://legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=112073' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Eviction is by summary rule to show cause before a court of competent jurisdiction; the rule must state the grounds. (La. C.C.P. Art. 4731(A); <a href='https://www.legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=112078' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Lessor may retake possession without judicial process on a reasonable belief of abandonment after notice; failure to comply gives a residential lessee the greater of $500 or twice monthly rent. (La. C.C.P. Art. 4731(B),(C); <a href='https://www.legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=112078' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Louisiana?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Louisiana houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/louisiana-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Louisiana Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/louisiana-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Louisiana Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/louisiana-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Louisiana guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-louisiana/'>We buy houses in Louisiana</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=112073' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>La. C.C.P. Art. 4701</a></li><li><a href='https://www.legis.la.gov/legis/Law.aspx?d=112078' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>La. C.C.P. Art. 4731(A)</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Louisiana Eviction Notice Rules, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https:/